# CTF-01 surface registration source proposal

Status: SOURCE-READY; ignored source proposal only. No canonical edits, formatter,
compiler, test, engine, import, scientific result or binary reads were performed.
Root retains the genuine failed production comparison and owns all execution.

## Source cause and change

Native SurfaceGeometry::GetSurfaceData calls CreateMissingSpaces at 1443, then
registers actual Surface array elements by Zone (1469), each Zone's spaceIndexes
(1470), BaseSurfIDs (1506), and stable SurfaceTmp order (1508-1528).
SurfaceGeometry.hh 549 fixes BaseSurfIDs as Wall, Floor, Roof.
GetHTSurfaceData 3918-3920 maps Ceiling to Roof. The separate legacy
AllSurfaceListReportOrder is not the Surface array registration order.

RawModel already preserves BuildingSurface:Detailed IDF declaration order;
direct epJSON retains its ordinary map order. This proposal leaves RawModel
unchanged and adds the missing final compiler registration permutation after
successful CreateMissingSpaces. Stable sort retains original relative order
within each actual Zone/Space/class group. It retains every Surface object,
reassigns zero-based SurfaceIds, and rebuilds both NameMap lookup and name order.
An unavailable owning group or duplicate normalized registration name is an
explicit internal compile error; no record is dropped or guessed.

## Prior SurfaceId association audit

At this point the only SurfaceId holders are Surface.id, surface_names, and
local explicit_space_assignments (compiler 13944-13997). The latter is fully
consumed by CreateMissingSpaces before registration and is not published.
Surface outside_boundary_condition_object is a NormalizedName, not SurfaceId;
Zone stores SpaceIds, and Space has no cached SurfaceId list. Material,
Construction, Zone, Space, boundary names, vertices and scalar fields move
with each unchanged Surface object. Surface-dependent typed vectors start
empty (model.rs 409-415). Variable absorptance bindings, solar attachments and
vapor attachments are constructed only after parse_surfaces (compiler711-745).
ModelGraph is created later from final typed owners (model.rs558-561/609-615).
No stale ID remapping of an earlier published consumer is therefore required.

## Scope and proposed verification

Only ordinary opaque BuildingSurface:Detailed Wall/Floor/Roof/Ceiling owners
already admitted by this compiler are affected. This does not port shading,
air boundaries, internal mass, windows, generated interzone surfaces, or new
Native surface families. It changes registration identity/order, not physics,
comparison sorting, precision profiles, frozen inputs, or observation masks.

Two focused tests are proposed, not executed: (1) mixed classes under direct
and IDF-overlaid input, stable same-class declaration order, unchanged raw
order, complete sequential IDs/name ledger, real downstream vapor attachment
and graph references; (2) multiple Zones and authored/remainder/default Spaces,
with Space grouping before class grouping and no lost or duplicated owner.
Existing error-barrier tests continue to cover skipping registration when
surface parsing fails. Root should run the focused module then relevant
compiler/package tests and rerun the original frozen production comparison.

